SUMMARY:Art Loeb at BRP to Pilot Mtn - 6.3 Mi\, 1900 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 6 Miles\, 2000 Ft
  elevation gain\n* Carpool meeting time is 8:00 at the Asheville Tanger Ou
 tlets parking lot behind the Waffle House.\n* Sign up starts Friday at 8pm
 \n\nI am going to try this hike again although the weather currently doesn
 't look promising for up in that area on Monday. This is a nice out and ba
 ck along the Art Loeb trail to Pilot Mountain which has a beautiful view a
 t the turn around. Some of the trail is a bit overgrown although not bad a
 nd I recommend long pants. We will keep a moderate pace dependent on the t
 errain but with limited stops. **Although the distance and elevation might
  sound like a moderate hike\, most of the elevation gain comes in the last
  1.5 miles. It felt like a much harder hike when I scouted because of that
  so please don't sign up unless you are okay for a challenge at the end wi
 th no way to go but up**.\n\nI enjoy stopping at the Pisgah Inn after the 
 hike and sitting in the rocking chairs behind the hotel. They have a conve
 nience store where you can buy drinks and sandwiches or you can bring your
  own. We will try to break up into cars that want to do that and want to j
 ust go back to the carpool area.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/cust
 om-routes/uploaded-route-72e4032\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will meet at the Ashev
 ille Outlets behind the Waffle House at 8:00. It is about a 50 minute ride
  to the trailhead. Please be there a little early so we can leave at 8:00 
 for the trailhead. There is very limited parking at the trailhead and it i
 s all along the side of the road. If you plan to meet us at the trailhead\
 , plan to be there by 8:50. See the AllTrails link above for directions to
  the trailhead.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and post a cancella
 tion message by 7:00 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation.\n
 \n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 9:00 AM the day 
 of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text or call me up 
 to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville 
 Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and 
 from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety an
 d affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, e
 quipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property.
  Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your sa
 fety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for 
 any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315605913
 /
