SUMMARY:Sleepy and Rainy Gap Loop 6.7 Miles\, 1300 Ft
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis is a good rainy day loop in B
 ent Creek starting from the Sleepy Gap Overlook parking area. We can make 
 the loop longer or shorter depending on what people want to do and how rai
 ny it is. I don't hike in a lightning storm but it doesn't look like that 
 is in the forecast for tomorrow morning. Bring your rain gear and this is 
 an umbrella friendly trail for those that like to use one.\n\nPlanned hike
  that we may adjust.\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/slee
 py-gap-loop-6-7-mile-cfb32ef\n\n**CARPOOL**\nNo carpool planned for this h
 ike as I figure you would rather control the mud in your own car. If you d
 o need to carpool from somewhere let me know.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch t
 he weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if there is a chance
  of lightning during this time period..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message
  me through MeetUp until 9:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy
 \, but you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 9
 65-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hikin
 g and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participant
 s are responsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appro
 priate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking m
 ay involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor 
 Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Par
 ticipants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losse
 s.
