SUMMARY:Coontree/Avery Creek Rd.  8 miles\, 1500' ascent
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Meeting Place:** **Mills River I
 ngles\, 3338 Boylston Hwy**: PLEASE NOTE: **Due to the hot weather\, I hop
 e to leave from Ingles at 8 AM**--\nDirections: I-26 Exit on NC-280 West\,
  Airport Road---4.3 miles to the Ingles on the right. Meet in front of gas
  pumps\, closest to Boylston Hwy. Mark's cell: 239-777-4743.\n**Details**:
  A challenging climb – almost all the ascent in 3.3 miles – up the wes
 t side of Coontree Loop\, then north on Bennett Gap past Coontree Mountain
 \, through open forest\, to Avery Creek Road. Returning on\nBennett Gap to
  an overlook with a snack break at 4.0 miles\, then down the east side of 
 Coontree Loop. Significant stretches of rough footing and rocks\, but good
  views of Looking Glass. Multiple (dry) crossings of\nCoontree Creek. Type
 : clockwise lollypop loop. Max elev: 3600’. Avg moving pace: 2.4 mph. Di
 fficulty (1=effortless\, 10=hard): 7 (with difficult stretches). Dogs: wel
 come if well-behaved and on a leash\, subject to area restrictions. **Ther
 e is the option of going for a beer/lunch after the hike**\n\n**Time:** We
 dnesday\, July 15. Prompt 8:00 departure from Mills River Ingles\n\n**Meet
 ing Place:** **Mills River Ingles\, 3338 Boylston Hwy---8:00AM** Direction
 s: I-26 Exit on NC-280 West\, Airport Road---4.3 miles to the Ingles on th
 e right. Meet in front of gas pumps\, closest to Boylston Hwy. Mark's cell
 : 239-777-4743. {Alternate meet spot--Coontree Picnic area on 176 at about
  8:20. Let me know if you're meeting there}\n**As always\, there is the op
 tion of lunch after the hike--Mills River Brewery?**\n\n**\\*\\*Courtesy**
  (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* pl
 an to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" 
 as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24 hours so that wait-liste
 rs can have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show
 .\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, p
 ossibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are res
 ponsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate sk
 ills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involv
 e risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville
  Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing u
 p for this event\, participant understands and agrees.
